          "uncertainty_type": 4\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      "process_description": "This is a Knoevenagel condensation reaction between ethyl cyanoacetate and benzophenone to produce etocrylene (ethyl 2-cyano-3,3-diphenylprop-2-enoate), a UV-absorbing compound used in cosmetics and sunscreens. Base-catalyzed Knoevenagel condensation (aldol-type reaction). Catalysts: Primary - Weak organic bases (piperidine, pyrrolidine, or secondary amines) or inorganic bases (K2CO3, Cs2CO3, or NaOH at catalytic quantities). Alternative: DBU (1,8-diazabicyclo[5.4.0]undec-7-ene) or other organocatalysts. Solvents: Polar aprotic solvents preferred - DMF, DMSO, or DMA (for faster reaction). Alternative: Methanol, ethanol, or toluene depending on scale and process economics. Reaction Conditions: Temperature 25-80°C (room temperature to moderate heating). Pressure: Atmospheric to slightly elevated. Duration: 2-24 hours depending on catalyst strength and temperature. Stoichiometry: 1:1 molar ratio. Mechanism: Base abstracts α-hydrogen from ethyl cyanoacetate to form reactive carbanion, carbanion attacks carbonyl carbon of benzophenone, hydroxyl intermediate forms and undergoes dehydration to yield conjugated product. Equipment: Jacketed reactor with mechanical stirring, reflux condenser, thermometer, addition funnel. Workup & Purification: Water removal by azeotropic distillation or vacuum distillation, product crystallization or column chromatography separation. Final purification typically yields >95% pure etocrylene. Industrial Applications: Etocrylene is a key intermediate/active ingredient in UV-absorbing cosmetic formulations (SPF products).",\\n      "uncertainty_type": 4\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  "root_node_id": "",\\n  "source": "SynthesisCompleter_agent",\\n  "uncertainty_type": 4\\n}\'}', 'level': 'info', 'logger': 'lciBuilder.CALLBACKS', 'timestamp': '2026-11-02 14:31:51'}
